# Keep the build context small and avoid shipping host-only artifacts into
# the image. Mirrors the exclusions in .gitignore plus Docker-specific ones.

# --- Version control / local tooling ---
.git/
.claude/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Secrets: never bake these into an image layer ---
# web_config.py is a PRIVATE, locally-edited file: its tracked/default
# content is just `os.environ.get("GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY", "")`, but a
# developer may locally paste a real key into it as the fallback default
# for convenience (its own docstring assumes it's gitignored, matching
# that workflow). Excluded here so whatever is currently sitting in a
# developer's local copy - secret or not - never ends up baked into an
# image layer that could later be pushed to a registry. The Dockerfile
# generates a safe, secret-free stand-in inside the image instead; pass
# the real key at `docker run` time with -e GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=...
web_config.py
.env
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# --- Big raw datasets: not needed at runtime, only for one-time preprocess.
# data/processed/ (the small generated artifacts) IS committed and IS
# needed at runtime, so it is intentionally NOT excluded here. ---
*.nc

# --- Non-runtime documentation (keeps the image smaller) ---
docs/*.pdf
docs/*.pptx

# --- Misc ---
*.log
.DS_Store
